**928**
* [**Removed**] NX-FanControl (overlay and system module), because fan control is now in KefirHub (Tools → Fan curve). When you open Fan curve, KefirHub offers to install its own fan module.
* [**Added**] [Atmosphere](https://github.com/rashevskyv/Kefirosphere) — disable individual system modules and SD mods through `system_settings.ini` ([PR #2901](https://github.com/Atmosphere-NX/Atmosphere/pull/2901)). The keys `disabled_contents`, `syscfw_disabled_contents` and `emummc_disabled_contents` in the `[atmosphere]` section accept up to 64 comma-separated ProgramIds. Example: `syscfw_disabled_contents = str!"0100000000001000"` disables custom themes on sysMMC only. Reboot after changes.
* [**Added**] [Hekate / Nyx](https://github.com/CTCaer/hekate) — backup hash validation before restore ([PR #1310](https://github.com/CTCaer/hekate/pull/1310)). The `verification=3` (Full Hashes) mode in `bootloader/nyx.ini` writes a `<name>.sha256sums` file during backup and checks it before restoring BOOT0/BOOT1, GPP or RAW GPP. A corrupted backup is not written to the eMMC. The default stays `verification=1`.
* [**Fixed**] [Atmosphere](https://github.com/rashevskyv/Kefirosphere) — the mesosphere kernel now saves all FPU registers of a thread when it switches the thread out during a user exception handler ([PR #2909](https://github.com/Atmosphere-NX/Atmosphere/pull/2909)). Before, the kernel saved only registers q8–q15, so the thread could continue with corrupted values after the handler. The fix affects homebrew and mods that install their own exception handler.
* [**Added**] [Hekate / Nyx](https://github.com/CTCaer/hekate) — support for Retro Remake SUPER5 and SUPER7 screens (IPS and OLED) ([PR #1314](https://github.com/CTCaer/hekate/pull/1314)). FHD versions run at their native 1080×1920 resolution, and the hekate and Nyx interface is scaled up from 720p. Nyx shows the screen model in the console information.

